 # 5\. Distinguish Root Cause vs Trigger vs Impact

 This will make your answer sound much more senior.

 ### Trigger

 The team performed a configuration change that required XL-Release reinstallation.

 ### Impact

 XL-Release pods could not start, because the Persistent Volume Claims remained unbound.

 ### Technical root cause

 The required VPC endpoint had been deleted, breaking EC2-to-EFS connectivity and therefore storage provisioning.

 ### Process/root cause

 The cleanup activity did not sufficiently verify whether the VPC endpoint was still required by an active workload.

 ### Resolution

 A new VPC endpoint was created.

 ### Prevention

 Resource ownership/usage must be validated before cleanup, and housekeeping scripts need controlled testing and review.

 You can summarize this as:

```
Trigger:
Configuration change / XL-Release reinstall

        ↓

Impact:
XL-Release pods stuck in Pending

        ↓

Immediate cause:
PVC/PV provisioning failure

        ↓

Technical root cause:
EC2 → EFS connectivity broken

        ↓

Infrastructure root cause:
VPC endpoint deleted

        ↓

Process root cause:
Insufficient validation during cleanup
```

